Titanos
Copyright 2026 Preston Goode

Titanos is a standalone implementation inspired by the Generic Inference
Microservices architecture in Preston Goode's HM2 / HiveMind project.
It does not include or require the HM2 application.

It uses third-party libraries, installed separately for source use or included
in platform-specific application bundles, including PyTorch,
Transformers, Diffusers, FastAPI, and optionally Coqui TTS. Those projects and
model checkpoints retain their own licenses and notices.

NVIDIA PAIR is an optional external integration and is not bundled.
Ponytail by Dietrich Gebert informed the development and review workflow.

The four-locale selection/fallback behavior and a small set of matching UI
labels were adapted from the MIT-licensed HM2-UI / HiveMind UI project,
copyright (c) 2026 HiveMind contributors. Titanos uses an original vanilla
JavaScript catalog and does not include HiveMind's React/i18next runtime.

The API documentation view (/docs) is rendered by Swagger UI (swagger-ui-dist
5.33.0, Apache-2.0, Copyright 2020-2021 SmartBear Software Inc.), included
unmodified under src/titanos/web/ and served by Titanos itself, so the page
requests nothing outside the server's own origin; its LICENSE and NOTICE are retained under
tools/licenses/ and tools/licenses/vendored_assets.json records the pinned
upstream tarball. ReDoc is not included.

Studio's display face is Chakra Petch 1.000 (SemiBold and Bold Italic),
Copyright 2018 The Chakra Petch Project Authors
(https://github.com/m4rc1e/Chakra-Petch.git), licensed under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1. Latin subsets converted to WOFF2 are included under
src/titanos/web/fonts/ with the license as OFL.txt, and inlined into
src/titanos/web/style.css, which also carries the license text; a copy is
retained under tools/licenses/ and tools/licenses/vendored_assets.json records
the upstream files.

